apeutics.com", "founded_year": null, "description": "Viking Therapeutics is a clinical-stage biotechnology company advancing a next-generation portfolio of therapies for obesity and metabolic disease. We are developing treatments to help patients achieve meaningful, lasting improvements in health by treating obesity first. Our therapies are designed to support the long-term health benefits of weight loss, including cardiovascular health, improved physical function, and quality of life."}, "business": {"products": [{"name": "VK2735", "category": "Dual GLP-1/GIP receptor agonist", "status": "Phase 3 obesity studies", "description": "Potential first dual agonist available in both oral and injectable formulations; demonstrated compelling efficacy in clinical trials; may offer flexible treatment from initial weight loss to ongoing management."}, {"name": "VK3019", "category": "Amylin receptor agonist", "status": "Phase 1 study in healthy adults", "description": "Novel next-generation approach for obesity."}, {"name": "VK2809", "category": "Therapy for metabolic and liver diseases", "status": "Pipeline", "description": "Targeting metabolic and liver diseases."}, {"name": "VK0214", "category": "Pipeline candidate", "status": "Pipeline", "description": null}, {"name": "VK5211", "category": "Pipeline candidate", "status": "Pipeline", "description": null}], "services": [], "industries": [], "key_markets": []}, "financials": {"employee_count": null, "key_numbers": []}, "relationships": {"customers": [], "investors": []}, "intel": {"summary": "Viking Therapeutics is a clinical-stage biotech focused on obesity and metabolic disease. Lead asset VK2735 is in Phase 3, with a potential dual oral/injectable GLP-1/GIP agonist profile. The company is also advancing earlier-stage candidates including an amylin receptor agonist (VK3019) and programs for metabolic/liver diseases.", "actionable_insights": ["Track VK2735 Phase 3 readouts, as positive data could position Viking in the high-v