[Results Announcements][49]\n    * [Annual Reports][50]\n    * [Financials - Subsidiaries][51]\n    * [Related Party Transactions][52]\n  * [Shareholder Information][53]\n    * [Shareholding Pattern][54]\n    * [Buyback of shares][55]\n    * [Share Performance][56]\n    * [Financial Highlights][57]\n    * [Notice of Board Meetings][58]\n    * [General Meetings][59]\n    * [Dividend Record][60]\n    * [Scheme of Arrangements][61]\n    * [Unpaid Dividend Account Details][62]\n    * [Registrar and Share Transfer Agent][63]\n    * [Contact Details for Investor Grievance Redressal][64]\n    * [Special window for lodgement of physical shares][65]\n  * [Corporate Governance][66]\n    * [Board of Directors][67]\n    * [Governance Policies][68]\n    * [Code of Conduct][69]\n    * [Code of Practices and Procedures for Fair Disclosure][70]\n    * [Appointment and Resignation of Directors][71]\n    * [Contact Details of KMPs][72]\n    * [IR Contacts][73]\n  * [Disclosures Under Regulation 46][74]\n    * [Disclosures under Regulation 46 of the LODR][75]\n* [Media][76]\n  * [Press Releases][77]\n  * [Corporate Kit][78]\n* [Careers][79]\n  * [Our Culture & Values][80]\n  * [Life @ Aurobindo][81]\n  * [Work with us / Opportunities][82]\n* [Contact Us][83]\n[Slide 1]\n\n# Committed to Healthier Life\n\nAurobindo Pharma Ltd. is committed to making a difference in the lives of millions of people by\nmaking medicines affordable and accessible for them across the globe.\n\n[Read More >>][84]\n[Slide 2]\n\n# Hon'ble Prime Minister\n# Shri Narendra Modi\n\nInaugurated our flagship Penicillin-G Facility at Kakinada,\nAndhra Pradesh\n\n[Slide 3]\n\n# One of the largest\n# Pharmaceutical Company\n\nWith a portfolio of 830 US ANDAs fillings\n\n# Delivering high quality biosimilars\n\nWe have a strong and sustainable pipeline of high value biosimilar programs with a primary focus on\nOncology and Immunology therapeutic segments.\n\n[Slide 5]\n\n# Annual Report\n\nTo access the comprehensive details of our annual performance, please click the link below to view\nour annual report.\n\n[Slide 6]\n\n# Corporate Social Responsibility\n\nAurobindo Pharma Foundation, the philanthropic arm of Aurobindo Pharma Limited, strives to transform\nand uplift the lives of underserved communities.\n\n[Slide 7]\n\n# Crafting a Responsible Tomorrow\n\nAurobindo Pharma commits itself to creating a more equitable and inclusive society by supporting\nprocesses that lead to a sustainable transformation.\n\n[Slide 8]\n\n# Life @ Aurobindo\n\nThe culture at Aurobindo is one of learning, collaboration, inclusivity with unlimited opportunities\nfor our employees\n\nPreviousNext\n\n## A global footprint of excellence\n\n[Footprint"}}, "page_text": "[[Logo][Logo]][1] * [About Us][2] * [About Aurobindo][3] * [Vision / Mission][4] * [Milestones][5] * [R&D][6] * [Manufacturing][7] * [Management][8] * [Board of Directors][9] * [Our Presence][10] * [Our Business][11] * [APUSA ][12] * [Europe][13] * [Growth Markets][14] * [ARV][15] * [Overview][16] * [Key facts about HIV/AIDS][17] * [Products][18] * [Global Partners][19] * [Gallery][20] * [Corporate Video][21] * [Apitoria (API)][22] * [Eugia (Speciality products)][23] * [Curateq (Biosimilars) / Peptide ][24] * [Sustainability][25] * [ESG / Sustainability][26] * [ESG Profile][27] * [Sustainability Reports][28] * [BMW Reports][29] * [Social Accountability Standards][30] * [Social Compliance Certification][31] * [Sustainability of Social Accountability Standards][32] * [Human Rights Policy][33] * [Progressive Health and Safety Practices][34] * [Community Impact][35] * [Supply Chain Management][36] * [Supplier Code of Conduct][37] * [CSR][38] * [Aurobindo Pharma Foundation][39] * [CSR Policy][40] * [Annual Report][41] * [Gallery][42] * [Annual Action Plan][43] * [Impact Assessment Reports - CSR Projects][44] * [Access to Healthcare][45] * [PEPFAR program][46] * [Investors][47] * [Results, Reports & Presentations][48] * [Results Announcements][49] * [Annual Reports][50] * [Financials - Subsidiaries][51] * [Related Party Transactions][52] * [Shareholder Information][53] * [Shareholding Pattern][54] * [Buyback of shares][55] * [Share Performance][56] * [Financial Highlights][57] * [Notice of Board Meetings][58] * [General Meetings][59] * [Dividend Record][60] * [Scheme of Arrangements][61] * [Unpaid Dividend Account Details][62] * [Registrar and Share Transfer Agent][63] * [Contact Details for Investor Grievance Redressal][64] * [Special window for lodgement of physical shares][65] * [Corporate Governance][66] * [Board of Directors][67] * [Governance Policies][68] * [Code of Conduct][69] * [Code of Practices and Procedures for Fair Disclosure][70] * [Appointment and Resignation of Directors][71] * [Contact Details of KMPs][72] * [IR Contacts][73] * [Disclosures Under Regulation 46][74] * [Disclosures under Regulation 46 of the LODR][75] * [Media][76] * [Press Releases][77] * [Corporate Kit][78] * [Careers][79] * [Our Culture & Values][80] * [Life @ Aurobindo][81] * [Work with us / Opportunities][82] * [Contact Us][83] [Slide 1] # Committed to Healthier Life Aurobindo Pharma Ltd. is committed to making a difference in the lives of millions of people by making medicines affordable and accessible for them across the globe. [Read More >>][84] [Slide 2] # Hon'ble Prime Minister # Shri Narendra Modi Inaugurated our flagship Penicillin-G Facility at Kakinada, Andhra Pradesh [Slide 3] # One of the largest # Pharmaceutical Company With a portfolio of 830 US ANDAs fillings # Delivering high quality biosimilars We have a strong and sustainable pipeline of high value biosimilar programs with a primary focus on Oncology and Immunology therapeutic segments. [Slide 5] # Annual Report To access the comprehensive details of our annual performance, please click the link below to view our annual report. [Slide 6] # Corporate Social Responsibility Aurobindo Pharma Foundation, the philanthropic arm of Aurobindo Pharma Limited, strives to transform and uplift the lives of underserved communities. [Slide 7] # Crafting a Responsible Tomorrow Aurobindo Pharma commits itself to creating a more equitable and inclusive society by supporting processes that lead to a sustainable transformation. [Slide 8] # Life @ Aurobindo The culture at Aurobindo is one of learning, collaboration, inclusivity with unlimited opportunities for our employees PreviousNext ## A global footprint of excellence [Footprint] [Footprint] [Footprint] [Footprint] [Footprint] ## Our Key Subsidiaries [[curateq logo]][85] [[Apitoria logo]][86] [[eugia logo]][87] ## Delivering exceptional value to all our consumers worldwide #### [Manufacturing Prowess][88] Our 29 manufacturing facilities across the globe have a manufacturing capacities of 50+ billion formulations units and 19,000+ MT APIs. and have advanced vertical integration to produce finished formulation products at an affordable price. [ Read More >>][89] #### [Global Presence][90] We are present across 150+ global markets including the US, Europe and Growth Markets, and are ranked amongst the top 10*** generic companies across eight countries in Europe. [ Read More >>][91] #### [Research & Development][92] Steadfast in our commitment to innovation & research, we invest significantly in our R&D. 830 filings for ANDAs in the US, with 600+ approvals for the same. [ Read More >>][93] ## News & Updates Loading... ## STAY CONNECTED * Largest generic Pharma Company in the US (by Rx dispensed as per MAT March 2024) ** Global workforce including both permanent employees and contractual workers *** Source: IQVIA data MAT Q3 2024 [[Footer Logo]][94] REGISTERED OFFICE Plot no. 2, Maitrivihar, Ameerpet, Hyderabad-500038, Telangana, India. CORPORATE OFFICE Galaxy, Floors: 22-24, Plot No.1, Survey No.83/1, Hyderabad Knowledge City, Raidurg Panmaktha, Rangareddy District, Hyderabad - 500032, Telangana, India. * [About Us][95] * [Our Business][96] * [Sustainability][97] * [Investors][98] 