t": "Challengers"}, {"Company": "Dr. Reddy's Laboratories", "Website": "https://www.drreddys.com", "Founded": "Not publicly disclosed", "Headquarters": "Hyderabad, India, Its", "Continent / Geography": "APAC(India)", "Operational Presence": "India", "Ownership": "Not publicly disclosed", "Employees": "Not publicly disclosed", "Core Categories": "Not publicly disclosed", "Specialty Focus": "Developing biosimilar GLP-1 RAs", "Key Brands Represented": "Not publicly disclosed", "Retail / E-commerce / Both": "No", "Distribution Type": "Brand", "Contact Person": "", "Role": "Brand", "Email": "", "LinkedIn": "", "Office No.": "", "Country Code": "IN", "Region Code": "APAC", "Summary": "Dr. Reddy's Laboratories — channel participant (chatgpt_recall). Verify: Developing biosimilar GLP-1 RAs, owns/markets branded drugs.", "Data Sources": "google_ai", "Data Confidence": "Medium", "Quality Score": "3", "commercial_role": "Brand", "verify_confidence": "85", "_evidence_snapshot": {"source": "", "domain": "drreddys.com", "data": {"company": {"name": "drreddys.com"}, "business": {"products": [], "services": []}, "intel": {"summary": "[\n[Desktop Logo]\n][1]\n[Who we are][2]\n[About Us][3][Our Journey][4][Our Leadership][5]\n[What we do][6]\n[Generics][7][API & Services][8][Innovative Medicines][9][Consumer Health][10][Patient\nPrograms][11][Healthcare Professionals Programs][12]\n[How we work][13]\n[Our Capabilities][14][Sustainability][15]\n[Work with us][16]\n[People & Culture][17][Careers][18]\n[Investors][19]\n[Contact Us][20]\n\n### Country Sites\n\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nAustralia][21]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nAustria][22]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nBrazil][23]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nCanada][24]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nChile][25]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nChina][26]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nColombia][27]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nCzech Republic][28]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nDenmark][29]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nFinland][30]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nFrance][31]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nGermany][32]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nIndia][33]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nNetherlands][34]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nNew Zealand][35]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nNorway][36]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nPoland][37]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nPortugal][38]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nRomania][39]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nRussia][40]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nSlovakia][41]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nSouth Africa][42]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nSpain][43]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nSweden][44]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nSwitzerland][45]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nUK][46]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nUkraine][47]\n[\n[Ind Flag]\nUS][48]\n\n# Good Health Can’t Wait\n\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\n\n## We Aim to Touch Over 1.5 Billion \n## Patient Lives by 2030\n\n[learn more][49]\n\n## 0\n\nCountries\n\n## 0\n\nActive US Abbreviated New Drug Applications (ANDAs)\n\n## 0\n\nActive US Drug Master Files (DMFs)\n\n## ~0 Mn\n\nPatients Reached (FY'25)\n\n## 0\n\nActive EU Dossiers Filed\n\n## 0\n\nActive EU Drug Master Files (DMFs)\n\n## Our Core Businesses\n\nWe operate across four main segments: Generics (branded, unbranded, and biosimilars), API & Services\n(development, manufacturing, and research support), Innovative Medicines, and Consumer Health\nsolutions. We are also expanding our portfolio across therapies through in-licensing and partnering\nwith innovative companies across the globe.\n\n[\n\nGenerics\n\n][50][\n\nAPI & Services\n\n][51][\n\nInnovative Medicines\n\n][52][\n\nConsumer Health\n\n][53]\n[Learn More][54]\n[My photo]\n\n## Latest News\n\n[U.S. FDA approval for Rituximab biosimilar]\n\n\n###### U.S. FDA approval for Rituximab biosimilar\n\nThis marks an important milestone and strengthens our growing global biosimilars portfolio in the\nUnited States.\n\n[Read more][55]\n[Approval of Zytorvi® in South Africa image]\n\n###### Approval of Zytorvi® in South Africa\n\nThis expands access to modern cancer treatments for patients with recurrent or metastatic\nnasopharyngeal carcinoma (RM-NPC), a rare and aggressive form of head and neck cancer.\n\n[Read more][56]\n[First-to-market launch of Sugammadex Injection in the United States image]\n\n###### First-to-market launch of Sugammadex Injection in the United States\n\nDr. Reddy's launch of the product is on the first day of generic availability in the United States,\nunderscoring our commitment to execution excellence and supply reliability.\n\n[Read more][57]\n[NUZOLVENCE® (zoliflodacin) receives Thai FDA approval image]\n\n###### NUZOLVENCE® (zoliflodacin) receives Thai FDA approval\n\nA first-in-class antibiotic for uncomplicated urogenital gonorrhea, marks a significant milestone in\nexpanding access to innovative treatments in low-and middle-income countries (LMICs), particularly\nin addressing the growing challenge of antimicrobial resistance.\n\n[Read more][58]\n\n## Our Efforts in the Fight Against Cancer\n\n\"Our mission is to turn\nscientific possibilities into real hope,\naddressing urgent patient needs\nand helping improve lives.\"\n\n##### Dr. Murali Ramachandra,\n##### Chief Executive Officer, Aurigene Oncology\n\n[Aurigene Oncology-image]\n\n###### Aurigene Oncology\n\nDeveloping innovative treatments to improve the lives of people with cancer and inflammatory\ndiseases\n[Read More][59]\n\n###### Rituximab\n\nWe launched the world's first rituximab biosimilar in India in 2007 for Non-Hodgkin Lymphoma and\nRheumatoid Arthritis\n[Read More][60]\n\n###### Imatinib\n\nA small molecule, targeted cancer drug to treat Chronic Myelogenous Leukemia, a type of a cancer\nthat affect"}}, "page_text": "[ [Desktop Logo] ][1] [Who we are][2] [About Us][3][Our Journey][4][Our Leadership][5] [What we do][6] [Generics][7][API & Services][8][Innovative Medicines][9][Consumer Health][10][Patient Programs][11][Healthcare Professionals Programs][12] [How we work][13] [Our Capabilities][14][Sustainability][15] [Work with us][16] [People & Culture][17][Careers][18] [Investors][19] [Contact Us][20] ### Country Sites [ [Ind Flag] Australia][21] [ [Ind Flag] Austria][22] [ [Ind Flag] Brazil][23] [ [Ind Flag] Canada][24] [ [Ind Flag] Chile][25] [ [Ind Flag] China][26] [ [Ind Flag] Colombia][27] [ [Ind Flag] Czech Republic][28] [ [Ind Flag] Denmark][29] [ [Ind Flag] Finland][30] [ [Ind Flag] France][31] [ [Ind Flag] Germany][32] [ [Ind Flag] India][33] [ [Ind Flag] Netherlands][34] [ [Ind Flag] New Zealand][35] [ [Ind Flag] Norway][36] [ [Ind Flag] Poland][37] [ [Ind Flag] Portugal][38] [ [Ind Flag] Romania][39] [ [Ind Flag] Russia][40] [ [Ind Flag] Slovakia][41] [ [Ind Flag] South Africa][42] [ [Ind Flag] Spain][43] [ [Ind Flag] Sweden][44] [ [Ind Flag] Switzerland][45] [ [Ind Flag] UK][46] [ [Ind Flag] Ukraine][47] [ [Ind Flag] US][48] # Good Health Can’t Wait Your browser does not support the video tag. ## We Aim to Touch Over 1.5 Billion ## Patient Lives by 2030 [learn more][49] ## 0 Countries ## 0 Active US Abbreviated New Drug Applications (ANDAs) ## 0 Active US Drug Master Files (DMFs) ## ~0 Mn Patients Reached (FY'25) ## 0 Active EU Dossiers Filed ## 0 Active EU Drug Master Files (DMFs) ## Our Core Businesses We operate across four main segments: Generics (branded, unbranded, and biosimilars), API & Services (development, manufacturing, and research support), Innovative Medicines, and Consumer Health solutions. We are also expanding our portfolio across therapies through in-licensing and partnering with innovative companies across the globe. [ Generics ][50][ API & Services ][51][ Innovative Medicines ][52][ Consumer Health ][53] [Learn More][54] [My photo] ## Latest News [U.S. FDA approval for Rituximab biosimilar] ###### U.S. FDA approval for Rituximab biosimilar This marks an important milestone and strengthens our growing global biosimilars portfolio in the United States. [Read more][55] [Approval of Zytorvi® in South Africa image] ###### Approval of Zytorvi® in South Africa This expands access to modern cancer treatments for patients with recurrent or metastatic nasopharyngeal carcinoma (RM-NPC), a rare and aggressive form of head and neck cancer. [Read more][56] [First-to-market launch of Sugammadex Injection in the United States image] ###### First-to-market launch of Sugammadex Injection in the United States Dr. Reddy's launch of the product is on the first day of generic availability in the United States, underscoring our commitment to execution excellence and supply reliability. [Read more][57] [NUZOLVENCE® (zoliflodacin) receives Thai FDA approval image] ###### NUZOLVENCE® (zoliflodacin) receives Thai FDA approval A first-in-class antibiotic for uncomplicated urogenital gonorrhea, marks a significant milestone in expanding access to innovative treatments in low-and middle-income countries (LMICs), particularly in addressing the growing challenge of antimicrobial resistance. [Read more][58] ## Our Efforts in the Fight Against Cancer \"Our mission is to turn scientific possibilities into real hope, addressing urgent patient needs and helping improve lives.\" ##### Dr. Murali Ramachandra, ##### Chief Executive Officer, Aurigene Oncology [Aurigene Oncology-image] ###### Aurigene Oncology Developing innovative treatments to improve the lives of people with cancer and inflammatory diseases [Read More][59] ###### Rituximab We launched the world's first rituximab biosimilar in India in 2007 for Non-Hodgkin Lymphoma and Rheumatoid Arthritis [Read More][60] ###### Imatinib A small molecule, targeted cancer drug to treat Chronic Myelogenous Leukemia, a type of a cancer that affects the blood and bone marrow [Read More][61] ## Bringing Innovative Therapies to Patients ## ## Helping bring effective treatments to patients faster and at a lower cost to ease the burden of ## disease. [Loxoprofen] ###### Loxoprofen Skorolox is the first loxoprofen INN available in Russia. It is used to relieve symptoms of acute upper respiratory tract infections, and to treat musculoskeletal and postoperative pain. [Read More][62] [Beyfortus®] ###### Beyfortus® A novel drug launched in India to protect newborns and infants from lung infections caused by Respiratory Syncytial Virus in the first season of exposure. [Read more][63] [Colozo®] ###### Colozo® A USFDA-approved option for Chronic Idiopathic Constipation in adults, which acts on gut receptors to help support normal digestive function. [Read more][64] ## Accelerating Access to ## Affordable and Innovative Medicines ## ## Our latest launches that bring innovative solutions to patients across the world [Toripalimab-image] ###### Toripalimab The first immunotherapy approved by major global regulators for recurrent or metastatic nasopharyngeal carcinoma (RM-NPC). In India, it introduces immuno-oncology as a first-line treatment for RM-NPC in combination with chemotherapy. [Read More][65] [Bevacizumab-image] ###### Bevacizumab Our first biosimilar approved and launched in the UK. It is a treatment for several types of cancer, including colorectal, lung, brain, kidney, cervical, and ovarian cancers. Bevacizumab works by blocking a protein called VEGF, slowing the growth and spread of cancer. [Read More][66] [Lenacapavir-image] ###### Lenacapavir A long-acting, USFDA-approved treatment for HIV-1 infection. Our work with Lenacapavir supports our goal to expand HIV treatment and prevention, especially in high-burden regions. We aim to manufacture and commercialise Lenacapavir across 120 countries, in partnership with Gilead Sciences. [Read More][67] ## Helping Patients Navigate Their Treatment Journey [Learn More][68] [Vega Club] #### Vega Club A patient support program where gastroenterologists help people with ulcerative colitis better understand and manage Inflammatory Bowel Disease through personalised guidance on diet, exercise, and stress. [betaCare] #### betaCare An initiative in Germany providing useful health information to patients. It also offers certified online courses to improve patient care, and help them navigate treatment and the healthcare system. [Joint Health Revolution] #### Joint Health Revolution Sessions developed for individuals with osteoarthritis, designed to guide them in understanding effective joint care. These doctor-led sessions help patients learn about the right exercises, healthy habits and ways to manage pain, and stay active. [Learn More][69] \"Our partners trust us because we have a long standing reputation for doing the right thing, no matter what. We are committed to accelerating access to 1.5bn patients and it can only be done by working with innovative companies doing great work across the globe.\" ##### Deepak Sapra, CEO API & Services ## Partnerships That Improve Access to Good Health ## ## We work together with our partners to bring healthcare solutions across communities [Gates Foundation] ###### Gates Foundation Working to develop an injectable contraceptive for low and middle income countries, advancing women's health, improving family planning options, and reducing health inequities. [Read More][70] [Sanofi] ###### Sanofi Partnering to distribute pediatric and adult vaccines in India, expanding immunization coverage, and strengthening disease prevention. [Read more][71] [Alvotech] ###### Alvotech Collaborating to expand access to essential cancer therapies approved for more than 40 types of cancer, strengthening oncology care and supporting patients with high-burden diseases worldwide. [Read more][72] ## Innovating Through Deep Science Capabilities ## ## Our teams are solving complex challenges with science and technology, keeping patients at the ## core [Learn More][73] [Scientist in Spotlight with Dr. Subramanian Narayanaswamy imgae] Scientist in Spotlight with Dr. Subramanian Narayanaswamy \"Complex injectables like peptides are redefining patient care, and we’re at the forefront of that transformation.\" [Leader's POV with Dr. Murali Ramachandra imgae] Leader's POV with Dr. Murali Ramachandra \"We have a well-developed research pipeline in India, with a primary focus on cancer treatments.\" [Learn More][74] ## From Doing Less Harm to Maximal Good ## ## We continue working towards reducing our environmental footprint, addressing ecological risks ## from our operations, and are progressing towards carbon neutrality [Learn More][75] [Water] #### Environment ###### Water By implementing initiatives such as wastewater recovery, grey water use, and more, we reduced freshwater consumption by ~70,000 KL from April to September 2023. [Climate Risk Mapping and Scope 3 Reduction image] ###### Climate Risk Mapping and Scope 3 Reduction By conducting site-level climate risk assessments and improving supplier engagement by sustainable procurement, we identified key vulnerabilities and reduced Scope 3 emissions intensity by 31% since FY2023. [Waste Reduction through Process Efficiency image] ###### Waste Reduction through Process Efficiency By implementing cost improvement projects and strengthening site-level waste checks, we achieved 20-22% reduction in waste across 9 high-volume products. [Decarbonisation Through Renewable Energy image] ###### Decarbonisation Through Renewable Energy By replacing fossil fuels with biofuels in boilers and expanding solar, wind, and hybrid energy use, we reduced Scope 1 and 2 emissions by 33% vs FY2023. Energy-saving initiatives also helped avoid 8,073 tonnes of CO₂ and saved 7.75 million kWh in FY2025. [Learn More][76] ## Content Hub Discover the science behind our products and how we work towards making a difference in patients' lives [View All][77] [ [PDF] PDF Rituximab A chimeric monoclonal antibody (mAb) used to treat certain autoimmune diseases & cancer. ][78] [ [PDF] PDF Nimesulide A non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAIDs) class of painkillers ][79] [ [PDF] PDF Toripalimab Immuno-oncology drug for treatment of adults with nasopharyngeal carcinoma. ][80] [[My photo]][81] © 2026 Dr. Reddy’s Laboratories Ltd. All rights reserved. © 2026 Dr. Reddy’s Laboratories Ltd. All rights reserved. Manage Cookie Preferences [1]: / [2]: # [3]: https://www.drreddys.com/about-us [4]: https://www.drreddys.com/our-journey [5]: https://www.drreddys.com/meet-our-leadership [6]: # [7]: https://www.drreddys.com/generics [8]: https://www.drreddys.com/active-pharmaceutical-ingredients [9]: https://www.drreddys.com/novel-molecules [10]: https://www.drreddys.com/consumer-health [11]: https://www.drreddys.com/patient-programs [12]: https://www.drreddys.com/doctor-programs [13]: # [14]: https://www.drreddys.com/business-and-capabilities [15]: https://www.drreddys.com/our-people-and-our-citizenship/sustainability [16]: # [17]: https://www.drreddys.com/our-people-and-our-citizenship/humans-of-dr-reddy-s [18]: https://careers.drreddys.com/ [19]: https://www.drreddys.com/investor [20]: https://www.drreddys.com/contact-us [21]: https://www.drreddys.au/ [22]: https://www.drreddys.at/ [23]: https://www.drreddys.com.br/ [24]: https://www.drreddys.ca/ [25]: https://www.drreddys.cl/ [26]: https://www.drreddyschina.com/ [27]: https://www.drreddys.com.co/ [28]: https://www.drreddys.cz/ [29]: https://www.drreddys.dk/ [30]: https://www.drreddys.fi/ [31]: https://www.reddypharma.fr/ [32]: https://www.betapharm.de/ [33]: https://www.drreddys.in/ [34]: https://www.drreddys.nl/ [35]: https://www.drreddys.co.nz/ [36]: https://www.drreddys.no [37]: https://www.drreddys.pl [38]: https://www.drreddys.pt/ [39]: https://www.drreddys.ro/ [40]: https://www.drreddys.ru/ [41]: http", "discovery_snippets": [], "classify": {"summary": "Dr. Reddy's Laboratories — channel participant (chatgpt_recall). Verify: Developing biosimilar GLP-1 RAs, owns/markets branded drugs. | Developing biosimilar GLP-1 RAs | India | Hyderabad, India, Its", "role_description": "Brand"}}, "X Score": "48", "Y Score": "46", "Overall Score": "47", "Industry Category": "Healthcare / Pharmaceutical", "Quadrant": "Trailblazers"}, {"Company": "Pfizer", "Website": "https://www.pfizer.com", "Founded": "Not publicly disclosed", "Headquarters": "New York City, USA", "Continent / Geography": "NA(United States)", "Operational Presence": "United States", "Ownership": "Not publicly disclosed", "Employees": "Not publicly disclosed", "Core Categories": "Not publicly disc