No", "Distribution Type": "Brand", "Contact Person": "", "Role": "Brand", "Email": "", "LinkedIn": "", "Office No.": "", "Country Code": "IN", "Region Code": "APAC", "Summary": "Biocon Biologics — channel participant (openai_web_search_discover). Verify: Biocon Biologics markets liraglutide biosimilar in India, owning the brand.", "Data Sources": "google_ai", "Data Confidence": "Medium", "Quality Score": "3", "commercial_role": "Brand", "verify_confidence": "85", "X Score": "45", "Y Score": "47", "Overall Score": "46", "Industry Category": "Healthcare / Pharmaceutical", "Quadrant": "Challengers"}, {"Company": "Cipla", "Website": "https://www.cipla.com", "Founded": "Not publicly disclosed", "Headquarters": "Mumbai, India, Its", "Continent / Geography": "APAC(India)", "Operational Presence": "India", "Ownership": "Not publicly disclosed", "Employees": "Not publicly disclosed", "Core Categories": "Not publicly disclosed", "Specialty Focus": "Has GLP-1 RA biosimilar plans", "Key Brands Represented": "Not publicly disclosed", "Retail / E-commerce / Both": "No", "Distribution Type": "Brand", "Contact Person": "", "Role": "Brand", "Email": "", "LinkedIn": "", "Office No.": "", "Country Code": "IN", "Region Code": "APAC", "Summary": "Cipla — channel participant (chatgpt_recall). Verify: Has GLP-1 RA biosimilar plans, owns/markets branded drugs.", "Data Sources": "google_ai", "Data Confidence": "Medium", "Quality Score": "3", "commercial_role": "Brand", "verify_confidence": "85", "X Score": "48", "Y Score": "43", "Overall Score": "46", "Industry Category": "Healthcare / Pharmaceutical", "Quadrant": "Trailblazers"}, {"Company": "Intas Pharmaceuticals", "Website": "https://www.intaspharma.com", "Founded": "Not publicly disclosed", "Headquarters": "Gujarat, India, Its", "Continent / Geography": "APAC(India)", "Operational Presence": "India", "Ownership": "Not publicly disclosed", "Employees": "Not publicly disclosed", "Core Categories": "Not publicly disclosed", "Specialty Focus": "Intas has a presence in the Indian diabetes market and offers GLP-1 receptor agonists.", "Key Brands Represented": "Not publicly disclosed", "Retail / E-commerce / Both": "No", "Distribution Type": "Brand", "Contact Person": "", "Role": "Brand", "Email": "", "LinkedIn": "", "Office No.": "", "Country Code": "IN", "Region Code": "APAC", "Summary": "Intas Pharmaceuticals — channel participant (openai_web_search_discover). Verify: Intas offers GLP-1 receptor agonists in India, indicating brand ownership or marketing.", "Data Sources": "google_ai", "Data Confidence": "Medium", "Quality Score": "3", "commercial_role": "Brand", "verify_confidence": "80", "_evidence_snapshot": {"source": "", "domain": "intaspharma.com", "data": {"company": {"name": "intaspharma.com"}, "business": {"products": [], "services": []}, "intel": {"summary": "[ [logo] ][1]\n[search icon]\n* [About Us][2]\n  * [Overview][3]\n  * [Awards & Accolades][4]\n* [Business Operations][5]\n* [R & D][6]\n  * [Overview][7]\n  * [Platform Technologies][8]\n  * [Biologics Business Unit][9]\n  * [Centre of Cell & Gene Therapy][10]\n  * [Plasma Fractionation Centre][11]\n* [Manufacturing][12]\n  * [Overview][13]\n  * [Pharmaceuticals][14]\n  * [Biologics Business Unit][15]\n  * [Cell & Gene Therapy Centre][16]\n  * [Plasma Fractionation Centre][17]\n* [Products][18]\n* [Media][19]\n* [Contact][20]\n[ [logo] ][21] [ [logo] ][22]\n\n\n\n\n\n[ Previous ][23] [ Next ][24]\n\n### Intas is Officially a \"Great Place to Work\" Certified\n\nThis certification highlights our shared dedication to creating supportive, inclusive and engaging\nworkspace.\n\n### A Global Healthcare Partner\n\nIntas is trusted by healthcare professionals across more than 85 countries across the globe\n\n### A Dynamic Product Basket\n\nEmpowered by a passionate R&D Team, Intas has one of the strongest product portfolios in the world\n\n### Plasma Therapy for Life\n\n[>Click Here][25] to know more about India’s Leading Plasma Fractionation Centre\n\n## Intas Pharmaceuticals Ltd.\n\nIntas is one of the leading multinational pharmaceutical formulation development, manufacturing and\nmarketing companies in the world. Today, Intas is present in more than 85 countries worldwide and is\ngrowing at ~22% CAGR. Around 70% of its revenues come from the international markets, particularly\nthe highly regulated markets of EU and US. At Intas, every day and everyone works to create a world\nof good health, happiness and hope.\n\n[ Read More][26]\n\n### Excellence is a Matter of Fact\n\n#### $\n\nBillion Turnover\n\n#### %\n\nCAGR Growth\n\n#### #  \n\nGeneric Company in the UK\n\n#### +\n\nProduct Registrations Worldwide\n\n## Transforming Science into Smiles\n\n[Research and Development]\n\nR & D is at the heart of Intas’ success. A highly qualified team works round the clock with a quest\nto develop a progressive threefold product basket that includes world-class generics, oncology and\nparenteral as well as added-value products (AVPs).\n* **6-7%** of turnover invested in R & D, year on year\n* Over **1,00,000** sq ft dedicated R&D space\n* **550+** Scientists and Researchers\n* **17** Advanced Facilities\n* Global Regulatory Authority Accreditations\n* Pioneer in Biosimilars\n\n[read more][27]\n\n## Latest News\n\n[Media]\n12, December 2018\n\nINTAS launches THYMOTAS - a patented, powerful immuno-booster add-on to standard COVID-19 treatment\n\n[ Read More][28]\n[Media]\n12, December 2018\n\nINTAS Develops COVID-19 Hyperimmune Globulin - A New Treatment\n\n[ Read More][29]\n[Media]\n12, December 2018\n\nIntas Pharmaceuticals becomes the first to launch Romiplostim in India, revolutionizing chronic\nimmune thrombocytopenia (ITP) therapy.\n\n[ Read More][30]\n\n## Featured Products\n\n[\n[Globucel-VF]\n\n### Globucel-VF\n\n][31]\n[\n[Pro-throm]\n\n### Pro-throm\n\n][32]\n[\n[IntaGlob]\n\n### IntaGlob\n\n][33]\n[\n[Globucel-SC]\n\n### Globucel-SC\n\n][34]\n[\n[Fibrogen I]\n\n### Fibrogen I\n\n][35]\n[\n[Factocel IX]\n\n### Factocel IX\n\n][36]\n[\n[Factocel VIII]\n\n### Factocel VIII\n\n][37]\n[\n[Thymotas]\n\n### Thymotas\n\n][38]\n[\n[ROMY]\n\n### ROMY\n\n][39]\n[\n[ELEFTHA]\n\n### ELEFTHA\n\n][40]\n[\n[Epofit]\n\n### Epofit\n\n][41]\n[\n[Cloba]\n\n### Cloba\n\n][42]\n[\n[Zenoxa]\n\n### Zenoxa\n\n][43]\n[\n[Divaa]\n\n### Divaa\n\n][44]\n[\n[Globucel]\n\n### Globucel\n\n][45]\n[\n[Albucel]\n\n### Albucel\n\n][46]\n[\n[Folisurge]\n\n### Folisurge\n\n][47]\n[\n[Looz]\n\n### Looz\n\n][48]\n[\n[Terifrac]\n\n### Terifrac\n\n][49]\n[\n[Mabtas]\n\n### Mabtas\n\n][50]\n[\n[Bevatas]\n\n### Bevatas\n\n][51]\n[\n[Gabapin NT]\n\n### Gabapin NT\n\n][52]\n[\n[Levera]\n\n### Levera\n\n][53]\n[\n[Clavix]\n\n### Clavix\n\n][54]\n[\n[Veltam]\n\n### Veltam\n\n][55]\n[\n[Amtas]\n\n### Amtas\n\n][56]\n[\n[Ceftas]\n\n### Ceftas\n\n][57]\n[\n[Valprol]\n\n### Valprol\n\n][58]\n[\n[Rabium]\n\n### Rabium\n\n][59]\n[\n[Lipicure]\n\n### Lipicure\n\n][60]\n[\n[Hifenac P]\n\n### Hifenac P\n\n][61]\n[\n[Zoryl M]\n\n### Zoryl M\n\n][62]\n[\n[company-logo]][63]\n\n**Corporate Office**\n\nIntas Pharmaceuticals Ltd.\n\nCorporate House, Near Sola Bridge, S. G.\n\nHighway, Thaltej, Ahmedab"}}, "page_text": "[ [logo] ][1] [search icon] * [About Us][2] * [Overview][3] * [Awards & Accolades][4] * [Business Operations][5] * [R & D][6] * [Overview][7] * [Platform Technologies][8] * [Biologics Business Unit][9] * [Centre of Cell & Gene Therapy][10] * [Plasma Fractionation Centre][11] * [Manufacturing][12] * [Overview][13] * [Pharmaceuticals][14] * [Biologics Business Unit][15] * [Cell & Gene Therapy Centre][16] * [Plasma Fractionation Centre][17] * [Products][18] * [Media][19] * [Contact][20] [ [logo] ][21] [ [logo] ][22] [ Previous ][23] [ Next ][24] ### Intas is Officially a \"Great Place to Work\" Certified This certification highlights our shared dedication to creating supportive, inclusive and engaging workspace. ### A Global Healthcare Partner Intas is trusted by healthcare professionals across more than 85 countries across the globe ### A Dynamic Product Basket Empowered by a passionate R&D Team, Intas has one of the strongest product portfolios in the world ### Plasma Therapy for Life [>Click Here][25] to know more about India’s Leading Plasma Fractionation Centre ## Intas Pharmaceuticals Ltd. Intas is one of the leading multinational pharmaceutical formulation development, manufacturing and marketing companies in the world. Today, Intas is present in more than 85 countries worldwide and is growing at ~22% CAGR. Around 70% of its revenues come from the international markets, particularly the highly regulated markets of EU and US. At Intas, every day and everyone works to create a world of good health, happiness and hope. [ Read More][26] ### Excellence is a Matter of Fact #### $ Billion Turnover #### % CAGR Growth #### # Generic Company in the UK #### + Product Registrations Worldwide ## Transforming Science into Smiles [Research and Development] R & D is at the heart of Intas’ success. A highly qualified team works round the clock with a quest to develop a progressive threefold product basket that includes world-class generics, oncology and parenteral as well as added-value products (AVPs). * **6-7%** of turnover invested in R & D, year on year * Over **1,00,000** sq ft dedicated R&D space * **550+** Scientists and Researchers * **17** Advanced Facilities * Global Regulatory Authority Accreditations * Pioneer in Biosimilars [read more][27] ## Latest News [Media] 12, December 2018 INTAS launches THYMOTAS - a patented, powerful immuno-booster add-on to standard COVID-19 treatment [ Read More][28] [Media] 12, December 2018 INTAS Develops COVID-19 Hyperimmune Globulin - A New Treatment [ Read More][29] [Media] 12, December 2018 Intas Pharmaceuticals becomes the first to launch Romiplostim in India, revolutionizing chronic immune thrombocytopenia (ITP) therapy. [ Read More][30] ## Featured Products [ [Globucel-VF] ### Globucel-VF ][31] [ [Pro-throm] ### Pro-throm ][32] [ [I