er 2026, pending U.S. Drug Enforcement Administration scheduling. **A new chapter for narcolepsy type 1 (NT1) care and orexin science** We expect to make this first-in-class medicine available to the NT1 community by November 2026, pending U.S. Drug Enforcement Administration scheduling. Learn more ][143] ## Our Stories ## Our Stories [View all stories[Chevron right]][144] [ [An adult and a child reading a book in a forest] ### Driving innovation in plasma-derived therapies Driving innovation in plasma-derived therapies [Calendar] June 24, 2026 ][145] [ [lab worker] ### Setting a new testing standard in the battle against polio Setting a new testing standard in the battle against polio [Calendar] May 21, 2026 ][146] [ [Two women walking] ### Finding the Words: How an EoE Diagnosis Changed One Family’s Outlook Finding the Words: How an EoE Diagnosis Changed One Family’s Outlook [Calendar] May 18, 2026 ][147] [View all stories[Chevron right]][148] ## Recent News ## Recent News [View all news[Chevron right]][149] [ ### U.S. FDA Approves Takeda’s ORZEYFUL™ (oveporexton), the First and Only Medicine to Treat the ### Underlying Cause of Narcolepsy Type 1 U.S. FDA Approves Takeda’s ORZEYFUL™ (oveporexton), the First and Only Medicine to Treat the Underlying Cause of Narcolepsy Type 1 [Calendar]August 5, 2026 [Arrow right] ][150] [ ### Takeda Announces FY2026 First Quarter Results, Near-Term Launch Preparations and Pipeline ### Progress on Track Takeda Announces FY2026 First Quarter Results, Near-Term Launch Preparations and Pipeline Progress on Track [Calendar]July 30, 2026 [Arrow right] ][151] [ ### Takeda’s ORZEYFUL (oveporexton) Approved in China as First Orexin Agonist and Only Medicine to ### Treat Narcolepsy Type 1 Takeda’s ORZEYFUL (oveporexton) Approved in China as First Orexin Agonist and Only Medicine to Treat Narcolepsy Type 1 [Calendar]July 22, 2026 [Arrow right] ][152] [ ### Takeda’s Zasocitinib Demonstrates Consistent, High Rates of Skin Clearance Across the Body, ### Including Hard-to-Treat and High-Impact Sites, in Phase 3 Psoriasis Studies Takeda’s Zasocitinib Demonstrates Consistent, High Rates of Skin Clearance Across the Body, Including Hard-to-Treat and High-Impact Sites, in Phase 3 Psoriasis Studies [Calendar]July 16, 2026 [Arrow right] ][153] [View all news[Chevron right]][154] ## Learn more about Takeda ## Learn more about Takeda [ [People smiling] ### Join Us ### Join Us Work with globally diverse colleagues who are committed to challenging one another to achieve more together. Work with globally diverse colleagues who are committed to challenging one another to achieve more together. Learn more ][155] [ [Person presenting] ### Investors ### Investors Discover how we're unlocking growth potential through bold innovation and a robust pipeline. Discover how we're unlocking growth potential through bold innovation and a robust pipeline. Learn more ][156] [ [Person in lab] ### R&D ### R&D We’re translating cutting-edge science into therapies that address urgent patient needs and create new standards of care. We’re translating cutting-edge science into therapies that address urgent patient needs and create new standards of care. Learn more ][157] ## Sign up for investors newsletter ## Sign up for investors newsletter Stay up to date on financial results, corporate milestones and learn how we're delivering on our commitment to patients, our people and the planet [Sign up][158] [[Takeda]][159] * [ [LinkedIn] ][160] * [ [YouTube] ][161] * [Locations][162] * [Contact us][163] * [Careers][164] * [Financial Highlights][165] * [HCPs][166] * [Patients][167] This website provides information about Takeda's worldwide business. For specific information about our local markets, please use the [country selector][168]. This website provides information about Takeda's worldwide business. For specific information about our local markets, please use the [country selector](/worldwide). * [Terms and Conditions][169] * [Privacy Notic