h jobs ][114] * Life at J&J * [ Life at J&J ][115] * [ Employee benefits ][116] * [ Professional development ][117] * [ Employee stories ][118] * [ Inclusion ][119] * Our teams * [ Our teams ][120] * [ Cardiology, cardiovascular and electrophysiology ][121] * [ Data science ][122] * [ Immunology ][123] * [ Market access ][124] * [ Medical affairs ][125] * [ Neuroscience ][126] * [ Oncology ][127] * [ Orthopaedics ][128] * [ Surgical, robotics and digital ][129] * [ Technology and cybersecurity ][130] * [ Vision and ophthalmology ][131] * Locations * [ Our locations ][132] * [ North America ][133] * [ EMEA ][134] * [ Asia Pacific ][135] * [ Latin America ][136] * Early career programs * [ Early career programs ][137] * [ Apprenticeships ][138] * [ Internships ][139] * [ Co-ops ][140] * [ Leadership development programs ][141] * [ Jobs for graduate students, postgraduates and postdocs ][142] * How we hire * [ How we hire ][143] * [ Application tips ][144] * [ Hiring programs ][145] * [ Hiring FAQs ][146] * [ Join our Global Talent Hub ][147] * Our company * [ Our company ][148] * [ Our Credo & our purpose ][149] * [ Leadership ][150] * Social impact * [ Social impact ][151] * [ CareCommunity ][152] * [ Global health equity ][153] * [ Nursing ][154] * [ Impact Ventures ][155] * [ Environmental sustainability ][156] * [ ESG resources ][157] * Suppliers * [ Suppliers ][158] * [ Responsible supply base ][159] * [ Supplier-enabled innovation ][160] * [ Supplier resources ][161] * [ Our history ][162] * [ Policies and reports ][163] * [Media ][164] * [Contact][165] Show Search Search Query Clear Submit Search Dictate search request Listening... ### Search Results ### No Results See all results Sorry, I don't understand. Please try again [Researchers in a laboratory reviewing data on a laptop while working with test samples and scientific equipment.] # We’re tackling the world’s toughest health challenges [ Medicines & therapies ][166] Johnson & Johnson Innovative Medicine is leading where medicine is going. Patients inform and inspire our science-based innovations, which continue to change and save lives. With rigorous science and compassion, we confidently address the most complex diseases of our time and unlock the medicines of tomorrow. Healthcare areas include: Oncology, Immunology, Neuroscience and Cardiopulmonary. [ Oncology ][167] [ Immunology ][168] [ Neuroscience ][169] [ Cardiopulmonary ][170] [ Learn more ][171] [ Medical devices & technology ][172] Johnson & Johnson MedTech innovates at the intersection of biology and technology. With a focus on treating with pinpoint precision in the hardest-to-reach parts of the body, restoring anatomy and reimagining healing, our portfolio of smarter, less invasive, more personalized treatments is addressing the most complex health challenges. Healthcare areas include: Cardiovascular, Orthopaedics, Surgery and Vision. [ Cardiovascular ][173] [ Orthopaedics ][174] [ Surgery ][175] [ Vision ][176] [ Learn more ][177] ## Innovating in healthcare * [ [what-you-need-to-know-about-johnson-johnsons-second-quarter-2026-earnings-report-lede-0726.png] ][178] [Latest news][179] July 15, 2026 ### [What you need to know about Johnson & Johnson’s second-quarter 2026 earnings report][180] Check out this infographic breakdown of the company’s second-quarter performance, with highlights from its Innovative Medicine and MedTech businesses. [ Read more ][181] * [ [Close up on a person's eye ] ][182] [Innovation][183] July 7, 2026 ### [“We are in a golden age of cataract surgery”][184] Once considered a straightforward procedure to restore cloudy vision, cataract surgery has evolved into one of the most technologically advanced—and personalized—operations in modern medicine. Learn how Johnson & Johnson’s 25-year history of innovation is helping eye surgeons meet the moment. [ Read more ][185] * [ [Two professionals looking at a series of images on screens depicting vital signs, anatomy and a surgeon in the operating room. ] ][186] [Innovation][187] July 23, 2026 ### [How the Polyphonic™ AI Fund for Surgery QuickFire Challenge awardees are aiming to empower ### surgeons][188] Johnson & Johnson launched this competition with one goal: to accelerate the development of next-generation surgical technologies. Meet this year’s three awardees and learn about their innovations. [ Read more ][189] * [ [Person sitting on bed looking out window with disrupted sleep, illustrating residual symptoms of major depressive disorder despite antidepressant treatment] ][190] [Health & wellness][191] August 11, 2026 ## [When depression improves but patients still grapple with symptoms][192] Only one in three people with major depressive disorder achieves remission after their first antidepressant, leaving many to continue to experience life-impacting symptoms such as disrupted sleep, changes in weight and appetite and trouble concentrating. Learn why Johnson & Johnson is working to help more patients achieve remission. [ Read more ][193] * [ [View over the shoulder of a researcher pipetting a medium into round dishes for multiple myeloma treatment research] ][194] [Innovation][195] June 1, 2026 ## [Striving for a cure for multiple myeloma: What HCPs need to know][196] Jordan Schecter, M.D., leader of Johnson & Johnson’s end-to-end development strategy for multiple myeloma, shares insight on the evolving treatment landscape of this rare blood cancer. [ Read more ][197] [ [Scientist in a lab coat and safety glasses working with samples under blue laboratory lighting.] ][198] ## Careers at J&J ### [Explore the latest job openings][199] [ Read more ][200] ### [Learn about our hiring programs ][201] [ Read more ][202] ### [Our career benefits][203] [ Read more ][204] ## Learn more about how we are innovating [ [Patient showing a plaque from plaque psoriasis on their elbow to their doctor] ][205] [Innovation][206] March 13, 2026 ### [5 things we now know about plaque psoriasis][207] Plaque psoriasis is the most prevalent form of psoriasis, affecting millions worldwide. Johnson & Johnson is focused on developing novel therapies for chronic dermatologic diseases to address the unmet need that still exists. [ Read more ][208] [ [Paul Reidy, Johnson & Johnson warehouse technician with multiple myeloma, at work and smiling at the camera] ][209] [Innovation][210] February 27, 2026 ### [“My company makes the medication that helped me fight multiple myeloma”][211] Paul Reidy, a Johnson & Johnson warehouse technician in Ireland, never imagined that an oncology therapy made at the facility where he works would help save his life. [ Read more ][212] [ [Closeup of a person using a pen to point at a monitor displaying brain scans for the purpose of studying schizophrenia] ][213] [Innovation][214] April 24, 2026 ### [“Reimagining what life with schizophrenia could look like”][215] Johnson & Johnson’s Leonardo Diaz, M.D., addresses common misconceptions about schizophrenia, the critical importance of preventing relapse and why there’s so much optimism about treatments. [ Read more ][216] [ [Deborah Borst, a lung cancer survivor, standing by the beach] ][217] [Health & wellness][218] June 4, 2024 ### [ “Lung cancer wasn’t even on my radar. Then I was diagnosed.”][219] The disease is often detected late—which can have fatal consequences. But thanks to innovations in diagnostic tools, there’s a way to catch lung cancer earlier. Here’s how early detection saved one woman’s life. [ Read more ][220] [ Back to top ][221] [ [johnson-johnson-logo-white-1.svg] ][222] * Discover J&J * [ News ][223] * [ Our Credo & our purpose ][224] * [ Leadership ][225] * [ Social impact ][226] * [ Suppliers ][227] * [ Our history ][228] * [ Policies & reports ][229] * [ Environmental sustainability ][230] * Medicines & therapies * [ Products ][231] * [ Oncology", "discovery_snippets": [], "classify": {"summary": "Johnson & Johnson — channel participant (chatgpt_recall). Verify: Has GLP-1 RA resea